# Conventional Commits

Every commit message in this repo uses Conventional Commits. semantic-release on `main` reads the subject to pick the version bump.

```
type(scope): subject
```

`scope` is optional. Subject is imperative, lowercase, and has no trailing period. Put the reason in the body when the subject is not enough.

```
fix: persist odds API quota to the DB instead of process memory

The in-memory counter reset on every pod restart, so the admin panel
showed an empty quota after each deploy.
```

Types that ship a release:

- `feat` — minor
- `fix`, `perf`, `revert` — patch
- `chore(deps)` — patch. Other `chore` commits do not release.

A breaking change is a major bump. Mark it with `!` after the type, and add a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer:

```
feat!: grade picks off the locked line

BREAKING CHANGE: picks no longer store spread_at_pick.
```

These types are valid and do not bump the version: `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, and `chore` without the `deps` scope.

Do not write `chore(release):` commits. semantic-release creates those.
